{
  "dom_id": "step-q106784",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** it is not winter, **then** Anna does not go skiing on Saturdays.",
  "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It is not winter.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ Anna does not go skiing on Saturdays.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬A⇒¬B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ It is winter.\n\n- $¬B:$ Anna goes skiing on Saturdays.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it is winter, then Anna goes skiing on Saturdays.",
